00:21:41,472 --> 00:21:46,408
-So, does Hardware Hank have a
major defense contract or...?

499
00:21:46,443 --> 00:21:49,791
-He's also a black belt
in "Whac-A-Mole."

500
00:21:49,825 --> 00:21:51,689
-[Grunts]
-Ha! That's neat!

501
00:21:51,724 --> 00:21:53,381
Welcome home, Nick!

502
00:21:53,415 --> 00:21:56,315
-You give up?! 
-Yes!

503
00:21:56,349 --> 00:21:58,213
-Now Nick's gonna
declare martial law,

504
00:21:58,247 --> 00:22:01,112
loot his museums,
and call in an air strike!

505
00:22:01,147 --> 00:22:03,943
♪♪

506
00:22:03,977 --> 00:22:06,635
-My hero!
-Ugh.

507
00:22:06,670 --> 00:22:08,672
-Wow.
-Whoa.

508
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:12,710
-Whew. You know, there hasn't
been such a glorious battle

509
00:22:12,745 --> 00:22:17,197
since the Arnold Stang/
Wally Cox fight of 1958.

510
00:22:17,232 --> 00:22:19,717
-You really humiliated me!
-Huh?

511
00:22:19,752 --> 00:22:21,995
-What? 
I didn't even want to do that!

512
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:23,756
-Oh, look! Ugh!
-Ew!

513
00:22:23,790 --> 00:22:26,483
-Ugh, ugh, ugh. 
-I wanted you to win.

514
00:22:26,517 --> 00:22:28,933
-How was I 
supposed to win, Amy?!

515
00:22:28,968 --> 00:22:31,108
I've never even 
done this before!

516
00:22:31,142 --> 00:22:33,662
It was an unfair match!

517
00:22:33,697 --> 00:22:35,768
-You looked really pathetic.

518
00:22:35,802 --> 00:22:37,563
-"Okay. Grab a rake!
Let's go!"

519
00:22:37,597 --> 00:22:39,634
-What do you want me 
to do for you?

520
00:22:39,668 --> 00:22:42,395
-I want you to make me proud.

521
00:22:42,430 --> 00:22:44,846
-Peewee Herman casual wear.

522
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:46,434
-They made love in a Chevy van,

523
00:22:46,468 --> 00:22:48,263
and that's not
all right with me!

524
00:22:48,297 --> 00:22:51,231
-Or me. 
-Give me that, Nick!

525
00:22:51,266 --> 00:22:54,234
[Rumbling]

526
00:23:05,487 --> 00:23:08,939
-Say, Mike, given the 
incrediblydepraved attitude

527
00:23:08,973 --> 00:23:10,872
regarding women
in today's movie,

528
00:23:10,906 --> 00:23:13,322
I knew you'd want me
to make a short film for boys

529
00:23:13,357 --> 00:23:16,498
and young men teaching them
how to treat the fairer sex

530
00:23:16,533 --> 00:23:19,950
with a proper
and healthy respect.

531
00:23:19,984 --> 00:23:21,883
Uh, Mike? Mike!

532
00:23:21,917 --> 00:23:24,299
-Uh, yeah, sure.
-So, uh, good 'cause

533
00:23:24,333 --> 00:23:26,405
I went ahead
and did it anyway,

534
00:23:26,439 --> 00:23:28,614
and hopefully
it'll help just a little.

535
00:23:28,648 --> 00:23:31,893
Let's watch.

536
00:23:31,927 --> 00:23:33,860
Ah, women.

537
00:23:33,895 --> 00:23:36,967
Women, women, women,
women, women, women, women.

538
00:23:37,001 --> 00:23:38,037
[Chuckles]

539
00:23:38,071 --> 00:23:40,142
For you young fellows
fresh on the cusp

540
00:23:40,177 --> 00:23:42,869
of a blooming manhood,
the questions abound.

541
00:23:42,904 --> 00:23:45,424
"What are women like?
What do women want?

542
00:23:45,458 --> 00:23:47,253
How should I treat a woman?"

543
00:23:47,287 --> 00:23:50,394
Perhaps the thorniest problem
facing any young man

544
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,707
is finding a woman
in the first place.

545
00:23:52,741 --> 00:23:57,401
It turns out
to be nearly impossible.

546
00:23:57,436 --> 00:24:00,887
This reporter spent countless
hours searching for a woman

547
00:24:00,922 --> 00:24:05,754
like these pictured here
to no avail.

548
00:24:05,789 --> 00:24:08,343
The nearest we came
during a tense stakeout

549
00:24:08,377 --> 00:24:13,141
was this fellow who experts
believe is nota woman.

550
00:24:13,175 --> 00:24:16,662
We begin to wonder,
where areall the women?

551
00:24:16,696 --> 00:24:18,871
The overheated references
in poetry,

552
00:24:18,905 --> 00:24:21,252
the images
that dominate our media --

553
00:24:21,287 --> 00:24:25,222
is it all an elaborate fraud?

554
00:24:25,256 --> 00:24:27,983
This grainy photograph
is the only direct evidence

555
00:24:28,018 --> 00:24:31,746
we have of a woman
in her natural environment.

556
00:24:31,780 --> 00:24:35,232
The longer hair, the gentle
and nurturing demeanor

557
00:24:35,266 --> 00:24:37,648
are typical
of how witnesses describe

558
00:24:37,683 --> 00:24:41,169
their supposed encounters
with women.

559
00:24:41,203 --> 00:24:44,517
This footprint, while possibly
the work of jokesters,

560
00:24:44,552 --> 00:24:46,415
is another piece of the puzzle,

561
00:24:46,450 --> 00:24:51,075
and it is hard to discount
this man's terrifying story.

562
00:24:51,110 --> 00:24:53,802
-And then, uh,
this woman, well,

563
00:24:53,837 --> 00:24:55,528
I think it was a woman.

564
00:24:55,563 --> 00:24:58,324
She, uh, married me.

565
00:24:58,358 --> 00:25:00,706
-Did you have any children, sir?

566
00:25:00,740 --> 00:25:03,363
-I don't remember!

567
00:25:03,398 --> 00:25:06,643
-Some day, perhaps,
an actual woman will emerge,

568
00:25:06,677 --> 00:25:08,265
and they will no longer exist

569
00:25:08,299 --> 00:25:11,924
only in the realm
of myths and maybe.

570
00:25:11,958 --> 00:25:14,064
Thank you.

571
00:25:14,098 --> 00:25:16,307
[Sighs]

572
00:25:16,342 --> 00:25:19,966
Oh, um, yeah, so, anyway, Mike,
in conclusion, um,

573
00:25:20,001 --> 00:25:23,487
in the off chance
that you do run into a woman,

574
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:26,663
uh, you know, treat her
with respect and stuff.

575
00:25:26,697 --> 00:25:29,010
-All right. You know, Crow,
you doknow women, though.

576
00:25:29,044 --> 00:25:30,839
What about Pearl?

577
00:25:30,874 --> 00:25:34,912
-Okay, so one woman exists.
That means allwomen exist?

578
00:25:34,947 --> 00:25:37,570
-We'll be right back.
-Name me one other woman.

579
00:25:37,605 --> 00:25:39,607
Go ahead.
-Well, I c--

580
00:25:39,641 --> 00:25:43,265
♪♪

581
00:25:47,131 --> 00:25:51,791
-What's the matter, Kevin?

582
00:25:51,826 --> 00:25:53,828
-"I got a 3 on the GED."

583
00:25:55,381 --> 00:25:58,453
-I-It's really a long story.

584
00:25:58,487 --> 00:26:00,524
-I've got all the time 
in the world.

585
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:05,046
-"Well, okay, then.
Call me Ishmael! I..."

586
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:09,602
-What do you do about someone 
who you can never make happy?

587
00:26:09,637 --> 00:26:11,708
-"Son, you make me very happy."

588
00:26:11,742 --> 00:26:14,124
-Is this your girlfriend 
we're talking about?

589
00:26:14,158 --> 00:26:15,781
-"No, I can't make
my hamster happy.

590
00:26:15,815 --> 00:26:18,162
What do you think?!" -I don't know what to tell you.

591
00:26:18,197 --> 00:26:19,681
What's the exact problem?

592
00:26:19,716 --> 00:26:22,408
-"Can I loosen her up for you?"

593
00:26:22,442 --> 00:26:25,998
-Well, w-we've got this friend 
who's in the Army.

594
00:26:26,032 --> 00:26:29,622
-"Omar Bradley?" 
-And my girlfriend's upset

595
00:26:29,657 --> 00:26:31,762
because I couldn't do 
all of the things that he can.

596
00:26:31,797 --> 00:26:35,145
-"Like join racist groups." 
-I see.

597
00:26:35,179 --> 00:26:38,079
Did I ever tell you what I did 
when I was in the Army?

598
00:26:38,113 --> 00:26:40,184
-"I was Tokyo Rose." 
-No.

599
00:26:40,219 --> 00:26:42,359
-Oh. It's also a long story.

600
00:26:42,393 --> 00:26:43,602
[Beeping]

601
00:26:43,636 --> 00:26:45,638
-"Oh. That'll be Kevorkian."

602
00:26:45,673 --> 00:26:50,643
-Uh-oh. Looks like 
we've got company.

603
00:26:50,678 --> 00:26:54,164
-Ah, some guy sneaking around
like a silent film villain.

604
00:26:54,198 --> 00:26:58,099
-Looks like Dana Gould.
-Huh.

605
00:26:58,133 --> 00:26:59,825
-Hey. 
-Wait here!

606
00:26:59,859 --> 00:27:02,172
I'll call you if I need you. 
-But, Mr. McCreedy!

607
00:27:02,206 --> 00:27:03,656
-I said wait!

608
00:27:03,691 --> 00:27:06,072
-"Turn on your baby-minder."

609
00:27:06,107 --> 00:27:10,732
♪♪

610
00:27:10,767 --> 00:27:13,873
-"Hey. 'The Kirk Cameron Show.'"

611
00:27:13,908 --> 00:27:16,669
-He goes the same speed
on the Ventura Freeway.

612
00:27:16,704 --> 00:27:19,534
♪♪

613
00:27:19,568 --> 00:27:22,226
-"Bullit." Now for seniors.

614
00:27:22,261 --> 00:27:25,747
♪♪

615
00:27:25,782 --> 00:27:27,991
-"I'll get that guy,
but first I'll just stop

616
00:27:28,025 --> 00:27:29,613
at the Bishop's Buffet here."

617
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,857
♪♪

618
00:27:31,891 --> 00:27:34,583
-♪ Take on me

619
00:27:34,618 --> 00:27:39,140
♪ Take me on

620
00:27:39,174 --> 00:27:41,694
-"Oh, I forgot
what I was doing!"

621
00:27:41,729 --> 00:27:44,317
♪♪

622
00:27:44,352 --> 00:27:46,975
-Ohh! Oh. 
-Shut up.

623
00:27:47,010 --> 00:27:50,116
-"Mm, I don't like the 'old guy
getting killed' channel."

624
00:27:50,151 --> 00:27:52,084
♪♪

625
00:27:52,118 --> 00:27:55,501
-"Nuh. If found, please return
to Hunter Thompson."

626
00:27:55,535 --> 00:27:57,330
♪♪

627
00:27:57,365 --> 00:28:01,265
-"I don't like the way
you greeted me at Walmart."

628
00:28:01,300 --> 00:28:04,510
-Get away from him.-"You Menendez brother wannabe!"

629
00:28:04,544 --> 00:28:08,238
-Who's this, your grandson? 
-No, h-he's my partner.

630
00:28:08,272 --> 00:28:10,999
-I said...

631
00:28:11,034 --> 00:28:12,414
-"Darn, what was it again
I said?"

632
00:28:12,449 --> 00:28:13,795
-...get away from him.
-"Yeah."

633
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:17,074
-Who you kidding? You don't know how to use that.

634
00:28:17,109 --> 00:28:21,596
-"All right. So I didn't
plug it in. You got me."

635
00:28:21,630 --> 00:28:23,011
-...marks. 
[Gunshot]

636
00:28:23,046 --> 00:28:25,807
-Aw, great, you just took out 
Air Force One,you dope.

637
00:28:27,498 --> 00:28:29,742
-[Coughs] 
-Are you okay?!

638
00:28:29,777 --> 00:28:31,226
Do you want me 
to call an ambulance?

639
00:28:31,261 --> 00:28:33,228
-No, no, I-I-I'm fine.

640
00:28:33,263 --> 00:28:35,403
-Damn! 
-What's the matter?

641
00:28:35,437 --> 00:28:36,991
-I just wish Amy 
could have been here

642
00:28:37,025 --> 00:28:38,440
to see what I just did!

643
00:28:38,475 --> 00:28:41,098
-"I shot a starter pistol
and whined out another line!"

644
00:28:41,133 --> 00:28:43,583
-He's still on the lot. 
-What do we do now?

645
00:28:43,618 --> 00:28:45,102
-I'm going to call the police.

646
00:28:45,137 --> 00:28:48,174
Try to locate where he is 
but keep a distance from him.

647
00:28:48,209 --> 00:28:50,245
Don't try to be a hero!

648
00:28:53,110 --> 00:28:55,906
-"I'd better call Grandma,
tell her I'm okay."

649
00:28:55,941 --> 00:28:58,806
[Rotary phone dialing]

650
00:28:58,840 --> 00:29:01,912
-"This is Captain Kangaroo.
Come in, Mr. Moose."

651
00:29:01,947 --> 00:29:05,157
♪♪

652
00:29:05,191 --> 00:29:07,124
-So, did the ad
for the job read,

653
00:29:07,159 --> 00:29:09,955
"Wanted --
whiny half-wit coward"?

654
00:29:09,989 --> 00:29:13,717
♪♪

655
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:15,892
-"I just want to be brave
for my horrible, frigid,

656
00:29:15,926 --> 00:29:17,997
nonsupportive girlfriend."

657
00:29:18,032 --> 00:29:21,104
♪♪

658
00:29:21,138 --> 00:29:24,486
-"When I find him, I'm gonna
make him sign in sobad."

659
00:29:24,521 --> 00:29:28,628
♪♪

660
00:29:28,663 --> 00:29:30,941
-"Serpico." "Dirty Harry."

661
00:29:30,976 --> 00:29:34,773
Jake Gittes.
-Kevin!

662
00:29:34,807 --> 00:29:37,568
-"This place is packed
with garden tools!"

663
00:29:37,603 --> 00:29:40,951
♪♪

664
00:29:40,986 --> 00:29:42,332
-Mr. McCreedy?

665
00:29:42,366 --> 00:29:44,748
-"Hello?! Hello?! Hello?"

666
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,474
-...where all the machinery is.

667
00:29:46,508 --> 00:29:48,614
-"No." 
-Think he went down there.

668
00:29:48,648 --> 00:29:50,685
I'm going in for a closer look.

669
00:29:50,719 --> 00:29:54,482
-"Hello. Who's this?"

670
00:29:54,516 --> 00:29:56,587
-Sit. Stay.

671
00:29:56,622 --> 00:29:59,798
♪♪

672
00:29:59,832 --> 00:30:01,420
-Carl Sandburg, P.I.

673
00:30:01,454 --> 00:30:03,802
-God. The vault!

674
00:30:03,836 --> 00:30:07,219
-"I've got to lobby against
Medicare cuts immediately!"

675
00:30:07,253 --> 00:30:10,878
-Kevin! 
Stop whatever you're doing!

676
00:30:10,912 --> 00:30:12,431
Don't go near the vault!

677
00:30:12,465 --> 00:30:15,020
No matter what you do, 
don't go near the vault!

678
00:30:15,054 --> 00:30:17,539
-This is Old Guy Radio, WOLD.

679
00:30:17,574 --> 00:30:21,095
-♪ W-O-L-D

680
00:30:21,129 --> 00:30:24,615
♪ The vault turned 21 in prison
doing life without parole ♪

681
00:30:24,650 --> 00:30:26,617
♪♪

682
00:30:26,652 --> 00:30:29,172
-Sister Kevin Prejean.

683
00:30:29,206 --> 00:30:32,313
-Amy. I want to make you proud.

684
00:30:32,347 --> 00:30:36,351
-"I'm gonna break into
Jack Benny's piggy bank."

685
00:30:36,386 --> 00:30:38,388
-And tell me again
why they have

686
00:30:38,422 --> 00:30:40,908
an elaborate security system
but they don't lock anything.

687
00:30:40,942 --> 00:30:43,634
-I don't know.

688
00:30:43,669 --> 00:30:46,327
-Ah, he's found
Ben Stein's money.

689
00:30:46,361 --> 00:30:47,915
-Hey.

690
00:30:47,949 --> 00:30:51,504
This is where the years
of mall walking pays off!

691
00:30:51,539 --> 00:30:54,887
♪♪

692
00:30:54,922 --> 00:30:57,890
-I mean, they don't even have
a twist tie on the door.

693
00:30:57,925 --> 00:30:59,409
Geez.

694
00:30:59,443 --> 00:31:02,446
-Script of "Billy Madison 2"
was kept hidden in here.

695
00:31:02,481 --> 00:31:06,899
♪♪

696
00:31:06,934 --> 00:31:09,039
-"Uh, what -- what am I doing?
Ow! Ow! Ooh!

697
00:31:09,074 --> 00:31:12,318
[Muffled] Crushed myself!
I'm crushed. I'm dead."

698
00:31:12,353 --> 00:31:16,667
-[Grunting] "Where did I leave
my egg-salad sandwich?! Ohh."

699
00:31:16,702 --> 00:31:22,639
♪♪

700
00:31:22,673 --> 00:31:27,471
-Hmm. Locked? Nah.

701
00:31:27,506 --> 00:31:29,957
-Buddy Ebsen, triathlete.

702
00:31:29,991 --> 00:31:36,895
♪♪

703
00:31:36,929 --> 00:31:39,725
-"Papillon? Hi.
The door was open."

704
00:31:39,759 --> 00:31:44,626
[Growling]

705
00:31:44,661 --> 00:31:46,352
-Oh, Taz got out.

706
00:31:46,387 --> 00:31:48,872
[Growling]

707
00:31:50,494 --> 00:31:52,531
-Oh, we're too late!

708
00:31:52,565 --> 00:31:55,120
Kevin, why did you go in there?

709
00:31:55,154 --> 00:31:56,638
Why didn't you listen to me?!

710
00:31:56,673 --> 00:32:00,125
-"Because you're really old. I
mean, would you listen to you?"

711
00:32:00,159 --> 00:32:02,713
-Enough with
the Count Chocula music!

712
00:32:02,748 --> 00:32:05,302
Geez!
-Take it easy. Take it easy.

713
00:32:05,337 --> 00:32:06,683
♪♪

714
00:32:06,717 --> 00:32:09,168
-"Come on.
Follow me to the band room."

715
00:32:09,203 --> 00:32:16,072
♪♪

716
00:32:18,281 --> 00:32:22,871
♪♪

717
00:32:22,906 --> 00:32:24,597
-What's going on?!

718
00:32:24,632 --> 00:32:27,531
-Ah, the hobgoblins.
Four hours in.

719
00:32:27,566 --> 00:32:28,877
-Yep.

720
00:32:28,912 --> 00:32:31,052
-What they done
with Casey Martin?!

721
00:32:31,087 --> 00:32:33,123
♪♪

722
00:32:33,158 --> 00:32:35,574
-♪ Oh, Thunder Road

723
00:32:35,608 --> 00:32:38,646
[Growling]

724
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:41,476
-"Yeah. A real smooth ride.
Good steering. I like it."

725
00:32:41,511 --> 00:32:45,894
♪♪

726
00:32:45,929 --> 00:32:48,828
-"I went to Michael Spinks'
barber, okay?!"

727
00:32:48,863 --> 00:32:51,797
♪♪

728
00:32:51,831 --> 00:32:54,006
-"Here. Try some pole dancing."

729
00:32:54,041 --> 00:32:57,044
♪♪

730
00:32:57,078 --> 00:33:00,737
-"They ripped out
the tape player!"

731
00:33:00,771 --> 00:33:04,568
-Oh. If you only knew 
what you just did.

732
00:33:04,603 --> 00:33:06,191
-Ooh! 
-I don't understand!

733
00:33:06,225 --> 00:33:09,228
What just happened?! 
-The vault!

734
00:33:09,263 --> 00:33:11,023
I-I tried to warn you.

735
00:33:11,058 --> 00:33:14,440
Those creatures. 
T-The vault. I tried.

736
00:33:14,475 --> 00:33:17,650
-Sentence fragments!
Just phrases!

737
00:33:17,685 --> 00:33:19,307
-All my work!

738
00:33:19,342 --> 00:33:22,897
30 years I've been trying to 
prevent this from happening.

739
00:33:22,931 --> 00:33:25,037
-To -- To prevent what 
from happening?!

740
00:33:25,072 --> 00:33:27,453
-T-Those creatures -- 
W-Why do you think

741
00:33:27,488 --> 00:33:30,767
I spent the last 30 years 
of my life here?!

742
00:33:30,801 --> 00:33:31,975
-Low SATs?

743
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:35,737
-I was keeping them 
from escaping!

744
00:33:35,772 --> 00:33:39,362
When I was young, 
I began to work here.

745
00:33:39,396 --> 00:33:42,572
The studio was -- 
was busy and prosperous.

746
00:33:42,606 --> 00:33:46,196
-"Now I sound like
Joseph Campbell."

747
00:33:46,231 --> 00:33:48,716
-I'll always remember 
the night that it happened.

748
00:33:48,750 --> 00:33:50,373
