01:25:28,709 --> 01:25:30,711
Could I use your phone?

1981
01:25:30,746 --> 01:25:32,575
-You know, Mike, one thing
I learned from this movie

1982
01:25:32,610 --> 01:25:34,129
is that Daphne is a slut

1983
01:25:34,163 --> 01:25:36,441
and Amy wasn't fun
until she became a slut.

1984
01:25:36,476 --> 01:25:37,960
-Oh, that's the fun
message of today.

1985
01:25:37,994 --> 01:25:39,375
-Oh, Mike?
A little help here.

1986
01:25:39,410 --> 01:25:41,170
-What's he up to?
-Yeah, what do you need?

1987
01:25:41,205 --> 01:25:42,965
-Come over here.
Rick Sloane's out here.

1988
01:25:42,999 --> 01:25:44,242
And he needs a little help.

1989
01:25:44,277 --> 01:25:45,485
-Rick Sloane?

1990
01:25:45,519 --> 01:25:47,418
-Yeah, Rick Sloane,
the director.

1991
01:25:47,452 --> 01:25:49,074
-He's here right -- right now?

1992
01:25:49,109 --> 01:25:51,215
-Yeah, the director
of today's movie, Rick Sloane,

1993
01:25:51,249 --> 01:25:53,665
wanted to explain
a few things about his film.

1994
01:25:53,700 --> 01:25:55,391
Hello?
Am I speaking English here?

1995
01:25:55,426 --> 01:25:56,634
Is it me?
-Geez, okay.

1996
01:25:56,668 --> 01:25:59,154
It just -- just seems
a little weird is all,

1997
01:25:59,188 --> 01:26:01,017
Rick Sloane actually being here.

1998
01:26:01,052 --> 01:26:03,365
-Well, he is.
-Oh. Oh, I see. Okay.

1999
01:26:03,399 --> 01:26:05,263
Yeah, yeah.

2000
01:26:05,298 --> 01:26:08,818
You know, Rick Sloane
is lighter than you'd thing.

2001
01:26:08,853 --> 01:26:10,095
-Oh.
Oh, is he, Mike?

2002
01:26:10,130 --> 01:26:12,546
Well, I guess I had
no preconceived notions

2003
01:26:12,581 --> 01:26:13,754
about Rick Sloane's weight.

2004
01:26:13,789 --> 01:26:15,549
I guess I'm not a racist
like you are, Mike.

2005
01:26:15,584 --> 01:26:17,379
-Hey.
-Boy.

2006
01:26:17,413 --> 01:26:21,797
-So, Rick Sloane, director
of "Hobgoblins," how are you?

2007
01:26:21,831 --> 01:26:23,661
-Crow!
-What?

2008
01:26:23,695 --> 01:26:25,594
-Perhaps you could be
of some assistance

2009
01:26:25,628 --> 01:26:27,078
in helping Mr. Rick Sloane

2010
01:26:27,112 --> 01:26:28,942
explain some of the things
about the film?

2011
01:26:28,976 --> 01:26:31,496
-Well, hey, he seems nice, but
I've never met the guy before.

2012
01:26:31,531 --> 01:26:33,118
-Would you just do
the voice, Crow?

2013
01:26:33,153 --> 01:26:34,913
-Oh, right, right, right.

2014
01:26:34,948 --> 01:26:36,915
-So, Mr. Rick Sloane.

2015
01:26:36,950 --> 01:26:38,572
-[Deep voice]
Hello, and how are you?

2016
01:26:38,607 --> 01:26:40,056
-Good, good.

2017
01:26:40,091 --> 01:26:42,473
Say, why don't you explain to
the good folks exactly what --

2018
01:26:42,507 --> 01:26:45,993
-Good. May I just say
how nice it is to meet you all.

2019
01:26:46,028 --> 01:26:48,375
My accommodations
are just lovely,

2020
01:26:48,410 --> 01:26:50,032
and everyone's been so nice.

2021
01:26:50,066 --> 01:26:51,413
Rarely have I been treated --

2022
01:26:51,447 --> 01:26:53,173
-Can we just please talk
about your film?

2023
01:26:53,208 --> 01:26:55,589
-Certainly, certainly.
My film, yes.

2024
01:26:55,624 --> 01:26:58,213
-Yes, yes, okay, when you
came up with the idea

2025
01:26:58,247 --> 01:27:01,906
for "Hobgoblins,"
were you high on crack?

2026
01:27:01,940 --> 01:27:03,942
Say yes.
-Yes, yes.

2027
01:27:03,977 --> 01:27:07,325
I had been doing quite a bit
of crack that day, as I recall.

2028
01:27:07,360 --> 01:27:08,464
-Yes, yes.
Good, good.

2029
01:27:08,499 --> 01:27:10,604
That helps me understand,
if just a bit.

2030
01:27:10,639 --> 01:27:12,365
Now, another question
I'm sure everyone

2031
01:27:12,399 --> 01:27:14,919
who has seen the movie
"Hobgoblins" has on their list,

2032
01:27:14,953 --> 01:27:17,853
and forgive me if I don't phrasethis in just the right way.

2033
01:27:17,887 --> 01:27:20,131
Are you, in fact, a total idiot?

2034
01:27:20,165 --> 01:27:22,271
Say yes.
-Yes, yes, I am an idiot.

2035
01:27:22,306 --> 01:27:23,548
That is correct.

2036
01:27:23,583 --> 01:27:25,895
How penetratingly intelligent
of you to notice.

2037
01:27:25,930 --> 01:27:27,380
-You know, Servo,
I couldn't help but notice --

2038
01:27:27,414 --> 01:27:28,898
-Stay out of it, Nelson.
-Okay, right.

2039
01:27:28,933 --> 01:27:31,315
-Now, director of this film,
Mr. Rick Sloane,

2040
01:27:31,349 --> 01:27:33,386
another question that
I've been asked to put to you

2041
01:27:33,420 --> 01:27:36,561
by the legions who've enjoyed
your film "Hobgoblins" --

2042
01:27:36,596 --> 01:27:38,287
Did someone open up your skull

2043
01:27:38,322 --> 01:27:41,117
and carefully replace
your brains with rat droppings?

2044
01:27:41,152 --> 01:27:42,774
Say yes.
-Yeah, I'm on it.

2045
01:27:42,809 --> 01:27:46,088
Yes, yes, once again,
your insight is quite correct.

2046
01:27:46,122 --> 01:27:47,538
I was home one night

2047
01:27:47,572 --> 01:27:50,782
right before the filming
of my hit film "Hobgoblins"

2048
01:27:50,817 --> 01:27:52,715
when I received
an unsolicited call

2049
01:27:52,750 --> 01:27:54,786
suggesting I try their service

2050
01:27:54,821 --> 01:27:58,134
wherein they replace my brains
with rat droppings.

2051
01:27:58,169 --> 01:28:00,240
It was a good deal,
so I said yes.

2052
01:28:00,275 --> 01:28:02,104
-Ah, good, good.
Another mystery solved.

2053
01:28:02,138 --> 01:28:03,588
Well, thank you for your time.

2054
01:28:03,623 --> 01:28:06,142
-Actually, Servo, I think you
have time for another question.

2055
01:28:06,177 --> 01:28:07,178
-Oh, really?

2056
01:28:07,212 --> 01:28:09,525
Uh, oh, gee,
I wasn't really prepared.

2057
01:28:09,560 --> 01:28:11,769
Um, well, Rick,
how are you, then?

2058
01:28:11,803 --> 01:28:14,358
-As I stated before, I'm good.
Thank you.

2059
01:28:14,392 --> 01:28:19,432
-Ah. Good.
So, Rick Sloane, good.

2060
01:28:19,466 --> 01:28:21,399
Do you have any hobbies at all?

2061
01:28:21,434 --> 01:28:22,711
-Nope.

2062
01:28:22,745 --> 01:28:24,609
-Really?
No -- No hobbies?

2063
01:28:24,644 --> 01:28:26,162
-None.
-Oh.

2064
01:28:26,197 --> 01:28:28,682
-Okay, you're off the hook.
We got to get out of here.

2065
01:28:28,717 --> 01:28:30,615
-Thank you.

2066
01:28:30,650 --> 01:28:32,237
-Bye, Rick.

2067
01:28:32,272 --> 01:28:38,209
♪♪

2068
01:28:38,243 --> 01:28:44,215
♪♪

2069
01:28:44,249 --> 01:28:47,149
-[Chuckles] Good work, Servo.
Nice job.

2070
01:28:47,183 --> 01:28:48,564
-Hey, clown.
-Hey, there, Mike.

2071
01:28:48,599 --> 01:28:49,945
You know how we really
didn't care

2072
01:28:49,979 --> 01:28:51,740
for that stupid movie today?
-Yeah.

2073
01:28:51,774 --> 01:28:53,569
-Well, by using
our time machine,

2074
01:28:53,604 --> 01:28:55,295
I went back to the early '80s,

2075
01:28:55,330 --> 01:28:58,125
and I took care of our
little Rick Sloane problem,

2076
01:28:58,160 --> 01:28:59,368
if you know what I mean.

2077
01:28:59,403 --> 01:29:02,337
-What? Servo, you don't --
you don't mean you --

2078
01:29:02,371 --> 01:29:03,752
-Yeah.
I sure did, Mike.

2079
01:29:03,786 --> 01:29:05,443
I hunted down Rick Sloane,

2080
01:29:05,478 --> 01:29:09,240
and I kicked him, Mike,
right in his shin!

2081
01:29:09,274 --> 01:29:11,069
I'm sorry, friend.
It's gruesome, I know.

2082
01:29:11,104 --> 01:29:12,761
But I had to take matters
into my own hands.

2083
01:29:12,795 --> 01:29:14,383
-Well, I thought, you know,
you'd gone back

2084
01:29:14,418 --> 01:29:16,212
and terminated him, you know?

2085
01:29:16,247 --> 01:29:17,317
-What do you mean, terminate?
Terminate?

2086
01:29:17,352 --> 01:29:18,387
What, are you -- are you nuts?

2087
01:29:18,422 --> 01:29:19,871
I hate guns!
I hate them!

2088
01:29:19,906 --> 01:29:21,666
How could you ever
get that idea? Man.

2089
01:29:21,701 --> 01:29:23,703
-I don't know.
-Well, anyway, by going back

2090
01:29:23,737 --> 01:29:26,533
and giving our Mr. Sloane
a firm, swift blow to the shin,

2091
01:29:26,568 --> 01:29:28,259
I have changed
the course of events,

2092
01:29:28,293 --> 01:29:29,812
and "Hobgoblins" is no more.

2093
01:29:29,847 --> 01:29:31,780
-[Normal voice] Hey! Hey!
Hey, hey, hey, you guys.

2094
01:29:31,814 --> 01:29:34,472
I'm doing my biography
of Rick Sloane here,

2095
01:29:34,507 --> 01:29:36,957
doing my research,
and listen to this.

2096
01:29:36,992 --> 01:29:40,029
Rick Sloane says the inspirationfor his film "Hobgoblins"

2097
01:29:40,064 --> 01:29:44,206
is like a stout red automaton
kicking him in the shins.

2098
01:29:44,240 --> 01:29:46,829
-Stout? Stout? He says stout?
That bastard.

2099
01:29:46,864 --> 01:29:48,279
I'm going back to kill him.
-No, no.

2100
01:29:48,313 --> 01:29:50,419
You know, I got to put a child
lock on our time machine.

2101
01:29:50,454 --> 01:29:51,869
-Good idea.

2102
01:29:51,903 --> 01:29:55,079
-Mike, Servo, Art,

2103
01:29:55,113 --> 01:29:57,599
I took away the couch
and brought it back down here.

2104
01:29:57,633 --> 01:30:00,049
-Whee!
-You are all old enough

2105
01:30:00,084 --> 01:30:03,156
to be taking some responsibilityfor some of our things.

2106
01:30:03,190 --> 01:30:05,503
Couches do not grow on trees.
-Whee!

2107
01:30:05,538 --> 01:30:07,540
-Hey, can I have some of
your Welch's grape juice?

2108
01:30:07,574 --> 01:30:09,438
-Sure, if I can have
some of that seal coat.

2109
01:30:09,473 --> 01:30:10,888
-You bet.

2110
01:30:10,922 --> 01:30:13,546
-There was a nice settee I was
thinking of sending up there.

2111
01:30:13,580 --> 01:30:15,513
There was a particular
office chair

2112
01:30:15,548 --> 01:30:17,584
I know you would have
enjoyed, Crow,

2113
01:30:17,619 --> 01:30:19,759
but I don't know that
I can ever trust you

2114
01:30:19,793 --> 01:30:23,107
with any home furnishings
ever again.

2115
01:30:23,141 --> 01:30:26,144
Bobo, Brain Guy,
who wants candy?

2116
01:30:26,179 --> 01:30:27,180
-Oh, I do!
-I do! I do!

2117
01:30:27,214 --> 01:30:29,320
-Me!
-Oh!

2118
01:30:29,354 --> 01:30:31,702
-I don't mean to yell.

2119
01:30:35,499 --> 01:30:37,915
[Explosions]

2120
01:30:37,949 --> 01:30:41,297
I just really want everyone
to stay off the couch.

2121
01:30:41,332 --> 01:30:42,954
-[Groans]

2122
01:30:42,989 --> 01:30:51,929
♪♪

2123
01:30:51,963 --> 01:31:00,938
♪♪

2124
01:31:00,972 --> 01:31:09,912
♪♪

2125
01:31:09,947 --> 01:31:18,887
♪♪

2126
01:31:18,921 --> 01:31:27,861
♪♪

2127
01:31:27,896 --> 01:31:36,801
♪♪

2128
01:31:36,836 --> 01:31:45,776
♪♪

2129
